<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Gerling unit buys French insurer.</title>
<headline>Belgian Gerling unit buys French insurer.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian credit insurance company Namur - Assurance du Credit said on Thursday it had acquired French insurer  Societe d'Assurance Credit des Entreprises (Sacren).</p>
<p>Namur said that together, Gerling, Namur and Sacren represented three billion Belgian francs of premium income in France, making them collectively the second biggest credit insurer in the country.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
